   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "image": "books/G1/099/p07.jpg",
   "w": 1400,
   "h": 549,
   "text": "In the Hive A home is called a hive. Many, many bees live in a hive. The inside of a hive looks like a lot of little boxes. The boxes are called cells.",
   "textBox": null,
   "wordBoxes": null,
   "audio": [
    43.62,
    51.43
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "image": "books/G1/099/p08.jpg",
   "w": 1400,
   "h": 549,
   "text": "The bees put the nectar into the little cells. Then lots of bees flap their wings very fast. This dries out the nectar and turns it into honey.",
